{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler-scaffold orchestrator) assigned task #5430: implement srd063-timeout requirements R3.1-R3.4 (Exit codes) in the go-unix-utils project. This is a stitch task in a code generation pipeline. The specific requirements are:\n   - R3.1: When command exits before timeout, exit with the command's exit status\n   - R3.2: When command is killed due to timeout, exit 124 (unless --preserve-status)\n   - R3.3: When command killed by signal not sent by timeout, exit 128+signum\n   - R3.4: When timeout itself fails (invalid args, command not found), exit 125/126/127\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/timeout/main.go` and `cmd/timeout/timeout_test.go`. Must verify with `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing against GNU `gtimeout` reference binary via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - Exit code semantics: 0 (success), 124 (timeout), 125 (internal error), 126 (command not executable), 127 (command not found), 128+N (killed by signal N)\n   - Process group management with `SysProcAttr.Setpgid`\n   - Signal handling (SIGTERM default, configurable via -s flag)\n   - Kill-after escalation (-k flag sends SIGKILL after delay)\n   - --preserve-status and --foreground flags\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Duration parsing with suffix multipliers (s, m, h, d) and fractional values\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd063-timeout.yaml`\n     - Source of truth for requirements. R3.1-R3.4 define exit code behavior. R4.1-R4.4 define test requirements.\n     - Key R3 requirements quoted above in section 1.\n   \n   - `cmd/timeout/main.go` (355 lines, existing implementation from R1-R2)\n     - Already contains exit code logic that appears to cover R3.1-R3.4:\n     - `exitCode` function (lines 90-114) handles signal detection and exit code mapping:\n       ```go\n       func exitCode(waitErr error, timedOut bool, opts options) int {\n           exitErr, ok := waitErr.(*exec.ExitError)\n           if !ok {\n               fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"timeout: %v\\n\", waitErr)\n               return 125\n           }\n           status, ok := exitErr.Sys().(syscall.WaitStatus)\n           if !ok {\n               return exitErr.ExitCode()\n           }\n           if status.Signaled() {\n               signum := int(status.Signal())\n               if timedOut && status.Signal() == opts.signal {\n                   if opts.preserveStatus {\n                       return 128 + signum\n                   }\n                   return 124\n               }\n               return 128 + signum\n           }\n           return exitErr.ExitCode()\n       }\n       ```\n     - `main` function (lines 27-53) handles command-not-found (127) and exec failure (126):\n       ```go\n       if err := cmd.Start(); err != nil {\n           if isNotFound(err) {\n               fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"timeout: failed to run command %q: %v\\n\", opts.cmdArgs[0], err)\n               os.Exit(127)\n           }\n           fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"timeout: failed to run command %q: %v\\n\", opts.cmdArgs[0], err)\n           os.Exit(126)\n       }\n       ```\n     - `parseArgs` returns exit code 125 for invalid arguments\n     - `runWithTimeout` returns 0 when `waitErr == nil` (command succeeded)\n   \n   - `cmd/timeout/timeout_test.go` (160 lines, existing tests from R1-R2)\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary` and `exec.LookPath(\"gtimeout\")` with skip\n     - Has `clearStderr` normalizer to ignore stderr differences\n     - Already has tests covering many R3.x scenarios:\n       - `command_completes_before_timeout` (exit 0) - R3.1\n       - `command_fails_before_timeout` (exit 1) - R3.1\n       - `command_exceeds_timeout` (exit 124) - R3.2\n       - `signal_hup` (exit 129) - R3.3\n       - `no_args` (exit 125), `missing_command` (exit 125), `invalid_duration` (exit 125) - R3.4\n       - `command_not_found` (exit 127) - R3.4\n       - `preserve_status_timeout` (exit 143) - R3.2 with --preserve-status\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - The existing implementation appears to already handle R3.1-R3.4 exit code logic from previous R1-R2 work. The task requires verifying completeness and adding dedicated/explicit R3.x test coverage. Potential gaps to address:\n     - R3.1: May need test for commands exiting with specific non-zero codes (e.g., exit 42)\n     - R3.3: May need a test where the child process kills itself with a signal (not sent by timeout)\n     - R3.4: May need test for command-not-executable (exit 126, permission denied scenario)\n     - The implementation may need minor refinements to ensure exact GNU compatibility\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The first message was the complete task description with all project context, SRDs, architecture, specifications, constitutions, and the specific task (#5430) to implement srd063-timeout R3.1-R3.4.\n   - The second message was: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement/verify R3.1-R3.4 in `cmd/timeout/main.go` (may need minor modifications or may be complete)\n   - Add dedicated differential test cases for R3.1-R3.4 in `cmd/timeout/timeout_test.go`\n   - Run `go build -o bin/timeout ./cmd/timeout/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/timeout/` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/timeout/... -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three key files (SRD, main.go, test file) and was about to begin the implementation/modification phase. I was analyzing the existing code to determine what changes are needed to fully satisfy R3.1-R3.4. The existing `exitCode` function and `main` function already implement the core exit code logic, so the primary work will likely be:\n   - Adding more specific/dedicated R3.x test cases (e.g., command exits with specific code like 42, child self-signals, permission-denied for 126)\n   - Possibly minor refinements to the implementation if any edge cases are found\n   - Building and running tests to verify\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Begin implementing the changes. Based on the task description: \"Implement srd063-timeout requirement R3.1-R3.4 as specified in the SRD\" and \"Add differential test cases covering R3.1-R3.4\". The existing code likely needs:\n   1. Review main.go for any gaps in R3.1-R3.4 logic (appears mostly complete)\n   2. Add explicit R3.x test cases to timeout_test.go - specifically:\n      - A test where a command exits with a specific non-zero code (e.g., `sh -c \"exit 42\"`) for R3.1\n      - A test where the child kills itself with a signal for R3.3\n      - A test for command-not-executable (126) for R3.4\n   3. Run build, vet, and test commands to verify all acceptance criteria\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5430/b8854d2c-587c-4d04-b6c4-9a7d2677a20e.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8854d2c-587c-4d04-b6c4-9a7d2677a20e","uuid":"ee668db1-aad4-4bba-be4f-4bca75dd0b99","timestamp":"2026-05